{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777934223,"nonce":"7fUI5sCRAuJXeVtSOm3sa4K8los=","title":"Phase 10: --ingest tar-entry preservation","message":"Currently --ingest treats stdin as an opaque byte stream.  When the input is a tar archive (the common case from the roadmap examples), we lose per-file boundaries -- restoration produces the original tar stream rather than the original tree.\n\nPhase 2 work: parse tar headers inline during ingest, emit one archive entry per tar entry, dedup CDC chunks within and across entries.  Restoration could either rebuild the original tar or extract directly via 'uc2 -x'.\n\nBuilds on v1 shipped at \u003ccommit\u003e.\n\nLabels: phase-10, P2-medium","files":null}]}